---
layout: layouts/base.njk
key: home
---

<h1 class="visually-hidden">Orcraft: test orchestration platform</h1>

<!-- Evaluation -->
<section class="section container text-center">
  <h2 class="section__title section__title--caps">Try it now:</h2>
  <div class="install">
    <code class="install__command">pip install orcraft</code>
    <button class="button button--ghost install__copy" type="button" data-copy="pip install orcraft"
      aria-label="Copy command" title="Copy command">
      <span class="install__copy-idle">{% icon "copy" %}</span>
      <span class="install__copy-done">{% icon "check" %}</span>
    </button>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Product preview -->
<section class="band">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section__title section__title--caps">How it works</h2>
    <div class="home-preview">
    <article class="card card--panel reveal">
      <button class="card__shot" type="button" data-lightbox aria-label="Enlarge screenshot">
        <img src="/assets/images/screenshots/build-tests.png"
          alt="Orcraft controller generating a test suite" loading="lazy" />
      </button>
      <h3 class="card__title">Develop tests with AI</h3>
      <p class="card__text">Generate a complete test suite from existing documentation sources. Suites can also be developed manually, or partially generated by AI.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card card--panel reveal">
      <button class="card__shot" type="button" data-lightbox aria-label="Enlarge screenshot">
        <img src="/assets/images/screenshots/configure-run.png"
          alt="Orcraft run configuration for GUI, CLI and CI" loading="lazy" />
      </button>
      <h3 class="card__title">Configure the run</h3>
      <p class="card__text">Configure once, then run it from the GUI or export it to run from the CLI or CI. No additional configuration files, scripts or plugins to maintain.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card card--panel reveal">
      <button class="card__shot" type="button" data-lightbox aria-label="Enlarge screenshot">
        <img src="/assets/images/screenshots/run-across-endpoints.png"
          alt="Orcraft controller running a session across endpoints" loading="lazy" />
      </button>
      <h3 class="card__title">Run across endpoints</h3>
      <p class="card__text">Run a suite, a group or a single test on the selected endpoints, in parallel. Re-run with different settings without touching the code.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card card--panel reveal">
      <button class="card__shot" type="button" data-lightbox aria-label="Enlarge screenshot">
        <img src="/assets/images/screenshots/logs-and-results.png"
          alt="Orcraft test group results with per-endpoint detail" loading="lazy" />
      </button>
      <h3 class="card__title">Analyze results with AI</h3>
      <p class="card__text">Turn the run's results into a report: failures, recurring patterns across endpoints and versions, and recommended actions.</p>
    </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Core capabilities -->
<section class="section container">
  <h2 class="section__title section__title--caps">Core capabilities</h2>
  <div class="capabilities">
    <article class="card card--feature">
      <span class="card__icon">{% icon "code" %}</span>
      <h3 class="card__title">Test development framework</h3>
      <p class="card__text">A defined structure, generated by AI or written manually: suites, groups, tests, cases, flows and steps in plain Python.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card card--feature">
      <span class="card__icon">{% icon "hierarchy" %}</span>
      <h3 class="card__title">Execution orchestration</h3>
      <p class="card__text">Build a run plan, queue sessions and execute cases in parallel across endpoints.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card card--feature">
      <span class="card__icon">{% icon "terminal-2" %}</span>
      <h3 class="card__title">GUI + CLI + CI</h3>
      <p class="card__text">Run the same suites from the controller, the command line or a CI pipeline.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card card--feature">
      <span class="card__icon">{% icon "world" %}</span>
      <h3 class="card__title">Remote &amp; shared endpoints</h3>
      <p class="card__text">An agent on remote machine, shared across the team. The developer defines the target endpoint per test step.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card card--feature">
      <span class="card__icon">{% icon "share-3" %}</span>
      <h3 class="card__title">Automatic upload &amp; updates</h3>
      <p class="card__text">Orcraft uploads the test package to each endpoint and updates its software whenever versions differ.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card card--feature">
      <span class="card__icon">{% icon "file-analytics" %}</span>
      <h3 class="card__title">Centralized logs &amp; results</h3>
      <p class="card__text">Every endpoint reports into one place: live logs, aggregated results and exportable reports for the entire run.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card card--feature">
      <span class="card__icon">{% icon "variable" %}</span>
      <h3 class="card__title">Parametrized cases</h3>
      <p class="card__text">Dimensions expand a test into a case matrix, executed in defined or randomized order over configurable cycles.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card card--feature">
      <span class="card__icon">{% icon "history" %}</span>
      <h3 class="card__title">Sessions &amp; history</h3>
      <p class="card__text">Sessions are saved, reopened later and re-executed with the same plan.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card card--feature">
      <span class="card__icon">{% icon "file-spreadsheet" %}</span>
      <h3 class="card__title">Reports &amp; export</h3>
      <p class="card__text">Spreadsheet reports, exportable session files and AI analysis for every run.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card card--feature">
      <span class="card__icon">{% icon "shield-lock" %}</span>
      <h3 class="card__title">Security</h3>
      <p class="card__text">Optional mTLS between controller and endpoints, with token-based access control.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Targeting / supported platforms -->
<section class="band">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="band__title">Targeting</h2>
    <ul class="pill-list">
      <li class="pill"><span class="pill__icon">{% icon "flask" %}</span>Validation labs</li>
      <li class="pill"><span class="pill__icon">{% icon "cpu" %}</span>Software, firmware and hardware validation</li>
      <li class="pill"><span class="pill__icon">{% icon "devices" %}</span>Cross-platform automation</li>
      <li class="pill"><span class="pill__icon">{% icon "infinity" %}</span>CI execution</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Supported platforms -->
<section class="section container">
  <h2 class="band__title">Supported on</h2>
  <ul class="audience-list">
    <li><img class="os-icon" src="/assets/images/os/os_windows.png" alt="" />Windows</li>
    <li><img class="os-icon" src="/assets/images/os/os_linux.png" alt="" />Linux</li>
    <li><img class="os-icon" src="/assets/images/os/os_macos.png" alt="" />macOS</li>
  </ul>
</section>
